  "notes": "The LA keyboard duo behind the teen-pop-meets-R&B template: 84–110 straight, backbeat on 2&4, and a documented harmonic cell — **Fm–E♭–D♭ (i–VII–VI)** in F minor at 84 BPM, \"a descending three-chord loop used in every section\" — so that family dominates and `maxChords` is 3. The drum signature is the entry's headline and the model's reason to exist: \"a **32nd-note bass-drum flutter** under the groove (a machine-gun sub-kick figure)… the kit is small and dry; **the flutter is the identity**\". There is no kick-subdivision field, so the flutter is authored as the only thing that reaches the generator — a kick `densityPerBar` of 4–9, the busiest in this section, at `syncopation` 0.46. The other two deltas are quoted: \"a 16th hat with an open hat on the last 8th\" (pinned 16ths, open hat on \"4&\" every bar) and \"claps stacked from the chorus\". The bass is deliberately negative space: \"synth bass on roots, short and staccato, **deliberately gapped so the kick flutter is audible**; no slides\", which is `independent_riff` at 0.9 with a low anticipation and no glide. The topline is \"melisma-heavy and sits in the lower third of the range in the verse before jumping to a sustained chorus apex\", with the range kept to about a 9th (F3–B♭4). ⚠ The **INFERRED** parameters are every drum probability; the key, cell, tempo, range, instrument roles and the drum signature are all sourced, the values are not.",
